course: dictionary
lesson: 2099
title: Continue: keep going, start again, go on
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Continue is a verb, and it has four main meanings: keep doing something without stopping, start again after a break, go further in the same direction, or keep existing. «If it continues, tell an adult» means if the problem keeps happening. The clue is the word it, which tells you that the problem is still going on.
explain: Read the words around continue to find the right meaning. «Continue with your work» means carry on with the task you already started. «Continue the pattern» in maths means find the next numbers by the same rule, such as 2, 4, 6, 8. Try your meaning in the sentence: if «keep going» makes sense, you have found the right one.
explain: Continue often appears in set phrases. «To be continued» at the end of a story part means the story goes on in the next part. A path can continue past a gate, and rain can continue all day. Look at the words after continue, such as «with», «to do» or «doing», because they often give you the clue.
fact: Continue is a verb: continue, continues, continued, continuing.
fact: «Continue» means to keep doing something without stopping.
fact: «Continue» can also mean to start again after a break, or to go on further in the same direction.
fact: «Continue the pattern» means work out the next numbers by the same rule.
fact: If a problem continues, it keeps happening.
exercise: «If a classmate's noise stops you working, you ask kindly first and tell the teacher if it continues.» In this sentence, what does continues mean? | It stops suddenly | *It keeps happening | It becomes a question | It is written down
exercise: Continue the pattern: 2, 4, 6, ... What are the next numbers? | 1, 2, 3 | 3, 5, 7 | Ten, twenty, thirty | *8, 10, 12
exercise: Mum says, «Please continue with your reading.» What does she want you to do? | Put the book away | Read the back cover only | Stop and go to bed | *Carry on with the reading you started
test: «To be continued» at the end of a story part means | The book is too long to read | The story has ended for ever | The teacher is cross with the class | *The story will go on in the next part
test: A path that continues past the gate means | The path is closed for ever | The path is made of stone | The path ends at the gate | *The path goes on further in the same direction
exam: Which sentence uses continue to mean start again after a break? | The rain will continue all night. | The path will continue past the gate. | *After lunch, we will continue our game.
